<title>UK: Williams shares up on H1 profit rise.</title>
<headline>Williams shares up on H1 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Williams Holdings Plc, the UK fire protection, security and building products group, posted modest gains in early dealings after the company reported a 11.4 percent rise in first-half pretax profits.</p>
<p>Williams rose two pence or 0.56 percent to 360p by 0707 GMT while the FTSE 100 index was indicated 0.31 percent higher.</p>
<p>Dealers said the results held few surprises and were in line with market expectations. Analysts had forecast pretax profits between 111 million stg and 118.9 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
